# 0113: wave64 decode wins on by default for 0.2.2 (XEON_MV_Q4K_V3=2, Q6_K repack)
#
# What. Two measured decode wins become the default on a 64-lane (wave64) card:
#   a. XEON_MV_Q4K_V3 unset -> value 2 (the no-shuffle 16-row Q4_K mat-vec). "0" -> off
#      (the pre-0.2.2 path). 1..4 unchanged. Anything else -> 2.
#   b. XEON_Q6K_REPACK unset -> on. "0" -> off. "1" -> on. Anything else -> on.
# Q4_K repack (XEON_Q4K_REPACK, 0112) is unchanged and stays off by default. When a Q4_K
# tensor is Q4_K-repacked, V3 is irrelevant for it (the repack twin owns the dispatch); that
# was already true and nothing here changes it.
#
# Why. Both arms were measured on card 1 and beat the 0.2.1 defaults on Q4_K_M decode with
# byte-identical text. 0111a (unfused QVK on wave64) is already default; this patch only
# flips the two remaining switches so a stock 0.2.2 launch gets the wins without env vars.
#
# Measured by orchestrator (engine v0.2.1-0112r2-avx1 = pin d81235049 + series through 0112,
# card 1 only, GGML_METAL_DEVICE_INDEX=1), llama-bench -ngl 99 -p 0 -n 128
# -fa 1, default context, arms alternating, warmup discarded by llama-bench.
#   Qwen3-8B Q4_K_M: default 10.58 t/s; XEON_MV_Q4K_V3=2 + XEON_Q6K_REPACK=1 14.75 t/s (t07/q4rb2).
#   Qwen3-4B Q4_K_M: default 17.13 t/s; V3=2 + Q6K repack 17.55 t/s (t07/q4rb2).
#   LFM3-1.7B Q6_K:  Q6_K repack (variant 2) 32.8 -> 37.2-37.4 t/s (t07/rb4b).
#   256-token greedy text byte-identical in every arm: 4B 91b358aa, 8B 3757ac38, LFM3 82d29582.
#   Own build (engine v0.2.1-0113-avx1 = pin + series through 0113), evidence t07/d0113-c1, d0113-c0. Card 1,
#   same llama-bench line, 3 alternating rounds (pp512: -p 512 -n 0 -r 3, 2 rounds), warmup discarded by llama-bench.
#   Arms: D default; V0 XEON_MV_Q4K_V3=0; R0 XEON_Q6K_REPACK=0; F XEON_QVK_Q4K_W64_FUSE=1; OLD all three (0.2.1).
#     Qwen3-8B Q4_K_M tg128: D 14.737-14.747  V0 12.681-12.683  R0 12.863-12.864  F 13.993-13.997  OLD 10.223-10.224
#     Qwen3-4B Q4_K_M tg128: D 17.539-17.576  V0 17.128-17.132  R0 17.541-17.558 (no 4B Q6_K tensor is eligible:
#                            n_embd 2560)  F 16.882-16.889  OLD 16.642-16.645
#     pp512: 8B D 42.95-42.96, OLD 41.07-41.09; 4B D 86.54, OLD 86.43-86.45.
#   Correctness, card 1 AND card 0 (display card, user-approved): test-backend-ops -b MTL0 -o MUL_MAT 1857/1857 with
#   no env (18 Q6_K tensors repacked, raw-bytes check OK) and with all three opt-outs; -o GET_ROWS 232/232 both
#   (no GET_ROWS case reaches a repacked Q6_K tensor). 256-token greedy text identical across all arms and both cards:
#   4B 91b358aa, 8B 3757ac38 (card 1), LFM3 82d29582; 'q6k-repack: mark' 37 on the 8B and 71 on LFM3 by default, 0 with
#   XEON_Q6K_REPACK=0.
#
# Opt-outs. XEON_MV_Q4K_V3=0 restores the pre-0.2.2 Q4_K decode path. XEON_Q6K_REPACK=0
# restores the pre-0.2.2 Q6_K path (no repack). XEON_Q4K_REPACK stays off by default.
#
# Test gate. tests/test-backend-ops.cpp use_weight_context() now matches the engine: Q6_K repack
# is active unless XEON_Q6K_REPACK=="0"; Q4_K repack is active only when XEON_Q4K_REPACK=="1".
# So a stock `test-backend-ops -b MTL0` (no env) builds WEIGHTS contexts and exercises the
# repacked Q6_K layout that now ships; XEON_Q6K_REPACK=0 falls back to plain contexts.
diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-device.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-device.cpp
